==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|īnlāzen}}, from {{inh|de|goh|inlāzan}}. Equivalent to {{prefix|de|ein|t1=in|lassen|t2=to let}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈaɪ̯nˌlasən/|[ˈʔäe̯nˌläsn̩]}}
* {{audio|de|De-einlassen.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|ein.lassen<lässt#ließ,gelassen>}}

# {{lb|de|transitive|formal|of a person}} to [[let in]]; to [[admit]]; to grant entry
#: {{syn|de|hereinlassen|hineinlassen|reinlassen|[[Zutritt]] [[gewähren]]}}
#: {{ux|de|Trotz mehrmaligem Klopfen wurde er nicht '''eingelassen'''.|Although he knocked several times, he was not '''let in'''.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|chiefly of liquids, gases}} to [[introduce]]; to cause to enter a room or fill a [[container]], usually slowly
#: {{syn|de|einleiten}}
#: {{ux|de|Das Insektenvernichtungsmittel wird durch zwei Düsen '''eingelassen'''.|The insecticide is '''introduced''' through two nozzles.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|with {{m|de|Bad}}}} to [[draw a bath]]; to [[run a bath]]
#: {{ux|de|Er '''lässt''' sich ein Bad '''ein'''.|He '''is drawing''' himself a bath.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|chiefly|construction}} to cause to be [[embed]]ded in something; to [[recess]]; to [[inset]]
#: {{ux|de|Der Kühlschrank ist in die Küchenwand '''eingelassen'''.|The refrigerator has been '''recessed''' into the kitchen wall.}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to [[get into]]; to become [[involved]] in (especially something risky) {{+obj|de|:auf(acc)/:in(acc)}}
#: {{ux|de|Er hätte sich nicht auf dieses Geschäft '''einlassen''' sollen.|He shouldn’t have '''got into''' this deal.}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to become [[involved]] with someone (usually one who is “bad company”, or for something risky or immoral) {{+obj|de|:mit}}
#: {{ux|de|Er hat sich mit einer verheirateten Frau '''eingelassen'''.|He’s '''become involved''' with a married woman.}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive|formal|law|usually of a defendant}} to [[testify]]; to [[declare]]; to [[state]]
#: {{syn|de|aussagen}}
#: {{ux|de|Der Beschuldigte hat sich '''eingelassen''', das Haus nie betreten zu haben.|The accused has '''declared''' never to have entered the house.}}

